23:["$","$L35",null,{"faqs":[{"question":"What is Industrial IoT (IIoT), and is this hardware or software?","answer":"It's the software and integration layer. We connect your existing machines, sensors, and PLCs to an IoT platform, build the dashboards and analytics, and add AI predictive maintenance — on your cloud, vendor-neutral. We don't sell you hardware; we make the equipment you already run intelligent."},{"question":"IIoT vs IoT — what's the difference?","answer":"Consumer IoT is smart homes and wearables. Industrial IoT connects factories, machines, and infrastructure, where uptime, safety, and integration with OT systems (PLCs, SCADA, MES) matter. The stakes and ROI are higher, and the integration is harder — which is exactly what we specialize in."},{"question":"Do you integrate with my ERP, MES, or SCADA?","answer":"Yes. IIoT only pays off when the data reaches your decisions. We wire it into your ERP, MES, SCADA, and historian, and speak the protocols your machines use — MQTT, OPC-UA, Modbus, and more — so the floor and the office finally share one source of truth."},{"question":"How does IoT predictive maintenance work?","answer":"We stream sensor data — vibration, temperature, current — to the platform, then use anomaly detection and machine-learning models to flag a failing motor, bearing, or pump before it stops the line. You fix it on a schedule, not in an emergency, and cut unplanned downtime."},{"question":"How much does an industrial IoT project cost?","answer":"It depends on how many machines and lines, and your goals. We work three ways: Agentic Operations as a monthly productized service, a fixed-scope project priced up front, or a dedicated nearshore IoT team from $50 USD/hour. Senior nearshore costs a fraction of an OEM engagement — and you own everything we build."},{"question":"Is it vendor-neutral, and do I own the platform?","answer":"Yes to both. We're not tied to one OEM or cloud — connect any sensor, PLC, or platform (AWS IoT, Azure IoT, or your own). Your platform, dashboards, code, and data are yours, with no black-box lock-in. You can run it, extend it, or take it anywhere."}],"id":"faq","title":"What teams ask before connecting the floor.","fill":true}]
24:["$","section",null,{"data-reveal":true,"className":"border-b-hairline-soft py-20","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-mono text-label uppercase text-fg-muted [letter-spacing:var(--tracking-label)]","children":"Related services"}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"mt-4 font-display text-display-m font-bold text-fg","children":"Often paired with industrial IoT"}],["$","ul",null,{"data-reveal-stagger":true,"className":"mt-8 flex flex-col gap-4","children":[["$","li","data-analytics",{"children":"$L36"}],["$","li","custom-software-development",{"children":"$L37"}],["$","li","cloud-migration",{"children":"$L38"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-20 font-mono text-label uppercase text-fg-muted [letter-spacing:var(--tracking-label)]","children":"Learn more"}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"mt-4 font-display text-display-m font-bold text-fg","children":"From the blog"}],["$","$L39",null,{"posts":[{"title":"IIoT vs IoT: what's the difference?","slug":"iiot-vs-iot","category":"Guide","excerpt":"IIoT vs IoT comes down to stakes and scale: consumer IoT runs your home, while industrial IoT (IIoT) runs factories, energy grids, and supply chains where downtime costs money. Here's the real difference — and what it means for your build.","readMin":6,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/iiot-vs-iot-sensor.webp","imageAlt":"A rugged industrial sensor with cabling on factory machinery, illustrating IIoT vs IoT"},{"title":"Industrial IoT applications: 10 real-world use cases","slug":"industrial-iot-applications","category":"Insight","excerpt":"The 10 highest-ROI industrial IoT applications — from predictive maintenance to OEE and asset tracking — with what each one connects, monitors, and predicts on a real factory floor.","readMin":6,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/iiot-applications-floor.webp","imageAlt":"An engineer inspecting connected industrial machinery on a factory floor, real-world industrial IoT applications"},{"title":"How much does an industrial IoT project cost? (2026)","slug":"industrial-iot-cost","category":"Guide","excerpt":"Industrial IoT cost depends on how many machines you connect, how deep the analytics go, and who builds it. Here's a real 2026 breakdown of industrial IoT cost — pilot, platform, and predictive maintenance — and how nearshore changes the math.","readMin":6,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/iiot-cost-install.webp","imageAlt":"A technician installing a sensor on industrial equipment, the cost of an industrial IoT project"},{"title":"Industry 4.0 & the smart factory: a starting roadmap","slug":"industry-4-0-smart-factory-roadmap","category":"Guide","excerpt":"An Industry 4.0 smart factory connects your machines, surfaces real-time data, and uses AI to predict failures. Here's a practical, phased roadmap to get from disconnected machines to a smart factory — without a rip-and-replace.","readMin":7,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/iiot-industry40-smartfactory.webp","imageAlt":"Robotic arms in a modern smart factory, illustrating the Industry 4.0 smart factory roadmap"},{"title":"IoT predictive maintenance: how AI cuts downtime","slug":"iot-predictive-maintenance","category":"Guide","excerpt":"IoT predictive maintenance uses sensor data and AI to predict equipment failures before they happen — cutting unplanned downtime. Here's how it works, what it costs, and how to roll it out on your factory floor.","readMin":6,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/iiot-predictive-maintenance.webp","imageAlt":"A technician inspecting machine belts with a wrench, IoT predictive maintenance"},{"title":"What is Industrial IoT (IIoT)? (and what it costs)","slug":"what-is-industrial-iot","category":"Guide","excerpt":"What is Industrial IoT? IIoT connects your machines, sensors, and PLCs to software that monitors the floor and predicts failures before they cost you downtime. Here's how it works, how it differs from consumer IoT, and what a project actually costs.","readMin":6,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/iiot-what-is-cables.webp","imageAlt":"Connected cables and sensors on factory equipment, illustrating what Industrial IoT is"}],"className":"mt-8"}]]}]
